# Normalise every text file to LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# This is a correctness requirement, not a style preference. The failure-memory
# package pins byte-exact SHA-256 digests of checked-in fixtures
# (`_COMPATIBILITY_DIGESTS` in `akms_failure_memory/ci.py`, and
# `test_compatibility_fixture_exact_bytes`). A Windows checkout with the default
# `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites those fixtures to CRLF, changing their bytes and
# their digests, so the drift detector fires on files nobody edited.
#
# The repository tracks no binary files today; add explicit `binary` entries
# above this rule if that changes.
* text=auto eol=lf
